{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And she departs and becomes another man's.</b> Even if the latter had with her nothing more than a mere betrothal — she became betrothed to him — the first husband may not take her back, since it is written <b>והיתה</b> (and she became). But if after he divorced her she committed adultery, her husband is permitted to take her back, as is proven in Sotah, chapter היה מביא. And what do I fulfill by 'asher heta'mi'ah'? To include a woman who commits adultery under her husband — who is forbidden to him."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:54:03.832223567Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}